{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted","id":1484541,"title":"Humanity and Morality! Opinions Wanted.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-20T13:18:12-07:00","id":1484541,"title":"Humanity and Morality! Opinions Wanted.","content":"I've been thinking about Humanity and the Paths of Enlightenment for a while now. Namely how to change it in a new and unique way. After some time, I came to the conclusion that I need some ideas and feedback. So here are a few questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Which edition's Humanity/Morality systems did you like best? Why?</li> <li>What do you think Humanity should represent?</li> <li>Do you like what Chronicles did with Integrity? Do you think it would be a good replacement for Humanity in VTM?</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T14:13:34-07:00","id":1484545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted#post1484541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about Humanity and the Paths of Enlightenment for a while now. Namely how to change it in a new and unique way. After some time, I came to the conclusion that I need some ideas and feedback. So here are a few questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Which edition's Humanity/Morality systems did you like best? Why?</li> <li>What do you think Humanity should represent?</li> <li>Do you like what Chronicles did with Integrity? Do you think it would be a good replacement for Humanity in VTM?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. V20<br /> 2. This is a complex one, I'd say we're inevitably affected by the &quot;Christian paradigm&quot; of how a &quot;good person&quot; should act/be, it's not easy deviating from this rule, Christian ethics still deeply influences our world view and what defines a good person, etc. From this point, I'd say Humanity represents how close to this idealized vision of human the vampire is/acts.<br /> 3. Sorry, but I don't know what this &quot;integrity&quot; means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T14:28:42-07:00","id":1484547,"title":"","content":"Integrity is what humans use as a score in Chronicles of Darkness Revised. Like a vampire's Humanity, it reflects how a mortal character is holding it together in a world that tries to drive them crazy or make them do terrible things to survive.<br /> <br /> I like it, and I like what Vampire: Requiem 2nd Edition does with Humanity as well. Both are impacted by what the character is exposed to as well as what the character has actively done, and the resulting combination stat for morality *and* sanity (in the Call of Cthulhu sense of sanity as a game mechanic) just works better for the Humanity score's stated intended purposes in Vampire the Masquerade. Your ability to remember your higher self and interact with society are impacted by the trauma you inflict on yourself, but also by just what living in the World of Darkness does to a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 06-20-2022, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T15:52:38-07:00","id":1484554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484547#post1484547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity is what humans use as a score in Chronicles of Darkness Revised. Like a vampire's Humanity, it reflects how a mortal character is holding it together in a world that tries to drive them crazy or make them do terrible things to survive.<br /> <br /> I like it, and I like what Vampire: Requiem 2nd Edition does with Humanity as well. Both are impacted by what the character is exposed to as well as what the character has actively done, and the resulting combination stat for morality *and* sanity (in the Call of Cthulhu sense of sanity as a game mechanic) just works better for the Humanity score's stated intended purposes in Vampire the Masquerade. Your ability to remember your higher self and interact with society are impacted by the trauma you inflict on yourself, but also by just what living in the World of Darkness does to a person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems fascinating, I must say. Requiem has many interesting concepts indeed, sometimes it makes me want to convert my vampire tables to Requiem. The thing that makes WoD interesting in fact is the metaplot (btw something they're managing to shit in V5...), because the system is mostly a mess, but the metaplot is probably the most interesting in any game I've played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T19:23:28-07:00","id":1484568,"title":"","content":"I think VtR 2e does such a good job because it has a strong design idea of what Humanity is supposed to mean (how well you character holds on to their previous existence as a human rather than a specific morality). The Bane system (you can take on additional traditional vampire folklore weaknesses to immunize yourself against certain Humanity checks) is also a more coherent way to cover the Path issue. Banes are not a get out of jail free card, because they increase your general detachment risks even if they help you with individual risks. You can make a character that vivisects humans to study the lines between life and death in order to try to understand the vampiric condition, without your Humanity dropping into the toilet, but it's a lot more work when you're not holed up in your &quot;laboratory&quot; and have to confront what you've become while trying to interact with people in a more normal way.<br /> <br /> I think for any of these sorts of mechanics, they work better when question #2 isn't really in the hands of the players. The game designers really need a strong idea of what these things should represent so that's never in question. Players might want to stress something else and implement house rules, but that's easier to do if you know what the base design is doing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T22:34:00-07:00","id":1484580,"title":"","content":"Answer to Question 2 in my game:<br /> <br /> &quot;the values of Humanity, understood as the core principles of respect for life and the adherence to common and natural laws, born during the Humanistic and Enlightened periods... Similar sets of values from non European universalist religions &quot;<br /> Also, a rejection of codes of conducts (Paths) that specifically view the vampire as an inhuman monster. <br /> So, individuals in the path of Humanity may have certain differences about specific issues (is stealing from a corporation theft? is death penalty for murderers acceptable? is your code defined by yourself, the community or God? ). But everyone should agree on fundamental issues.<br /> Now, if the ST wants to emphasize the differences, they can create different subpaths where the top of the hierarchy of sins is slightly different. For example, a socialist humanitarian would have greed as a sin, while a religious one would have not following religious tenet and a conservative pro capitalist theft or vandalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27429,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","user":"Microcuchon","date":". 06-21-2022, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T07:41:18-07:00","id":1484605,"title":"","content":"I like VtR 2e's version, because of what it represents, which Heavy Arms explained. I also like how there's no other way escape the Beast i.e. death inside. Paths offer the choice of self actualisation to those with the freedom to follow their own principles. VtR's elders have more to fear of what they may become, because they have less control.<br /> <br /> I don't know how Integrity works. In VtM, I think between paths and convictions, integrity, with a small i, is more important than morality or relating to humans anyway. And unlike in VtR, nearly every vampire has an elder who can challenge their integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T07:58:26-07:00","id":1484608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484580#post1484580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answer to Question 2 in my game:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;the values of Humanity, understood as the core principles of respect for life and the adherence to common and natural laws, born during the Humanistic and Enlightened periods... Similar sets of values from non European universalist religions &amp;quot;<br /> Also, a rejection of codes of conducts (Paths) that specifically view the vampire as an inhuman monster. <br /> So, individuals in the path of Humanity may have certain differences about specific issues (is stealing from a corporation theft? is death penalty for murderers acceptable? is your code defined by yourself, the community or God? ). But everyone should agree on fundamental issues.<br /> Now, if the ST wants to emphasize the differences, they can create different subpaths where the top of the hierarchy of sins is slightly different. For example, a socialist humanitarian would have greed as a sin, while a religious one would have not following religious tenet and a conservative pro capitalist theft or vandalism</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, VtM Paths are stupid. &quot;I wanna avoid turning into a mindless monsters, so I'll conciously turn into a mindful one&quot;. I mean, half of all published paths are worse than falling to the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:24:25-07:00","id":1484649,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>DAV20: I don't think it's right to say even normal humans in modern first world countries all follow the path of humanity, so I say the roads system fits much better. There are Real people out there who would have Not killing certain other people as one of their highest sins, path of humanity fails to be universal and function more like a &quot;Path of Christian Values&quot;.</li> <li>One possible path of morality among many equally valid approaches. Having one &quot;right&quot; morality makes A Lot of assumptions.</li> <li>Dunno, I've never played it.</li> </ol>On the fence about what I've heard about VTR. Marrying the VTM morality system with a Call-of-Cthulhu style Sanity system sounds cool and makes a lot of sense, but it also makes me cautious because sanity systems come with the inherent expectation that you're Meant to lose and I've met many a Dickish STs who would <i>Love</i> the power to take away player agency by throwing unpredictable San checks a players whenever that ST didn't like a discision someone made or the way the group was playing in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T15:27:14-07:00","id":1484659,"title":"","content":"I think calling it a full on CoC SAN system is going too far.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e largely works like Humanity in pre-V5 VtM. The big mechanical differences are:<br /> <br /> 1) Events beyond the players' control can trigger a check.<br /> 2) The level of the check directly relates to the number of dice you roll instead of the roll being based on a trait.<br /> 3) There's a more defined set of a modifiers (positive and negative) to the roll.<br /> 4) You get a Beat (XP) immediately every time you have to make a check, and you always get a Condition to resolve later for another Beat; high Humanity characters can easily get more XP with frequent checks than they lose buying any lost Humanity dots (though high risk/high reward strategy).<br /> 5) You can take extra Banes to permanently remove a breaking point from mattering to your character regardless of Humanity level.<br /> 6) Humanity is tied more directly to the severity of the Banes (both the main ones like fire and sunlight, Clan based ones, and opt-in ones), and things like torpor duration.<br /> <br /> While asshole STs will always find a way, it's pretty obvious if they're trying to do so in VtR 2e's setup. The more &quot;gotcha&quot; style breaking points tend to be very high Humanity (which mean you might not even have to roll anyway, and if you do you'll have a high dice-pool with low odds of failing so you're unlikely to lose Humanity this way), and really they're just feeding you XP more than they're going to force your Humanity into the ground if they try this sort of stuff. Below Humanity 6, the few remaining things a ST could try to &quot;spring&quot; on you quickly become a limited resource (such as the death of close family members, and it's pretty obvious if your ST keeps making up new family members you never detailed for your character to die), or aren't entirely in the ST's hands either (living extremely long amounts of time instigates a check, but the ST would have to be very rapidly fast forwarding the game by centuries for this to actually come up frequently).<br /> <br /> CofD vampires do not have to deal with &quot;holy shit, a monster!&quot; and risk losing Humanity. That's part of the Integrity system that mortals deal with.<br /> <br /> So, since nobody's really explained it:<br /> <br /> Integrity is the CofD's answer to &quot;are humans on Humanity?&quot; with a resounding, &quot;No.&quot; Integrity is a much looser system where breaking points are mostly individual based with some caveats to help keep the tone of the game in-tact (no sociopaths that get to be pure evil and still keep Integrity 10, but a character like Dexter Morgan could work to having a fairly decent Integrity score despite being a serial killer... it would be a challenge though).<br /> <br /> Rather than a moral code (though it can certainly include those) Integrity is mostly focused on how well a mortal maintains a sense of self and holds to their idealized version of themselves (there is, after all, a big difference between thinking your a good person and acting according to your standards for a good person) in the face of the Darkness that gives the setting its name. It's important to remember that part of the CofD's setting conceits is that mortals are in same ways aware they're in a supernatural world, but convince themselves that they're not. That's why being exposed to overt supernatural events ala CoC is a universal breaking point for mortals (otherwise they'd be something like a Hunter or worse that consciously accepts that supernatural monsters exist). So you get past different philosophies, cultural norms, and so on as each needing their own &quot;chart&quot; because mortals don't have a chart like that. And while there are good mechanical reasons to try to keep high Integrity and avoid low Integrity, you can't go NPC because of it. With enough work (and probably a lot of help) you can always recover Integrity even if you bottom out.<br /> <br /> As such a naive college student and a grizzled cop with twenty years on the streets are not going to roll for the same things (at least outside of major stuff like supernatural manifestations), or with the same modifiers. But that doesn't mean one is &quot;better&quot; than the other. Someone still figuring out who they are is less challenged by things that question more superficial aspects of their sense of self (switching schools sucks, but isn't likely to be a breaking point), but is less inured to the mundane cruelties of the world (having to use force even in self defense can easily be highly traumatic). Someone that defines themselves as their job as a cop is more set in certain things (that badge means something deep and personal to them, and leaving the force is a major blow even if they land a much better paying private security job in the process), but less bothered by things (they've seen the results of violence plenty of times before).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-21-2022, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T00:37:45-07:00","id":1484677,"title":"","content":"Here's my system (wip) The goal is to more accurately simulate morality and give players more freedom of choice. <br /> <br /> The Beast is kept at bay by ego. ego consists of both Conscience and Conviction. While you can choose one or the other depending on your path, most characters will have both. <br /> <br /> On Humanity/Conscience related paths. <br /> You accept all tenets for conscience, you choose your convictions. <br /> If you do something &quot;inhumane&quot;, you roll conscience<br /> If you do something &quot;inhumane&quot; in accordance with your conviction, you can add your conviction to the roll.<br /> If you do something against your convictions, you just roll conviction. <br /> <br /> On Conviction paths. <br /> You accept all tenets of your path for conviction, you choose what bothers your conscience. (you must choose something <br /> If you do something against your convictions, roll conviction. <br /> If you do something against your convictions in accordance with your conscience, roll both<br /> If you do something against your conscience, just roll conscience. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Other ideas I'm mulling over (but not sure of) <br /> Your willpower is based on your Courage+Conviction. (Or Courage+ the lowest of your conscience/Conviction?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T03:06:07-07:00","id":1484685,"title":"","content":"Accurately simulated morality is a fools errand since thousands of years of philosophy haven't exactly created rules around a general idea of what morality is to start to abstract and simulate. Trying to allow characters to simulate any morality system that a human can and has subscribed to would be extremely hard to do, and mostly just be a less fun and more cumbersome version of CofD 2e's Integrity mechanics in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T07:44:32-07:00","id":1484702,"title":"","content":"One nice thing about morality in a supernatural fictional setting is that you don\u2019t need to try and justify multiple belief systems about morality; the GM can just pick one that appeals to them and that is the Truth of that setting.<br /> <br /> If I choose \u201cThe Catechism of the Catholic Church is right about everything\u201d then people and vampires are only humane in relation to how well they adhere to those tenants. It doesn\u2019t matter if another religion says X is okay, if the CCC says it\u2019s immoral and a character does X then roll for Degeneration depending on where you are on the Hierarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> The reason I use the Catholic Church as an example is specifically because Bram Stoker included elements of faithful Protestants being told they had to use Catholic paraphernalia (i.e. crucifixes not crosses, communion wafers, rosaries, etc.) to have any hope of warding off a vampire and the character being told this becoming quite uncomfortable with the thought.<br /> <br /> Basically, in Bram Stoker\u2019s tale it didn\u2019t matter what the characters thought should or shouldn\u2019t work; the rules of the universe just were. I appreciate settings that aren\u2019t afraid to present a \u201cone true morality\u201d even if differs from my own. Having a specific truth instead of the \u201cwhatever you want to believe is true\u201d let\u2019s each tale be it\u2019s own spicy dish instead of a continual bland soup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T09:54:43-07:00","id":1484707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484702#post1484702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a specific truth instead of the \u201cwhatever you want to believe is true\u201d let\u2019s each tale be it\u2019s own spicy dish instead of a continual bland soup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely disagree. If you impose an external moral code to the PC's, all nuance and ethical discussion is thrown out of the window. How can you have a meaningful debate about whether it's ok to steal from a millionaire or to sentence a murderer to death when the &quot;objective truth&quot; is given by the setting and the rules? I prefer the nuance of my players having to choose what is valuable to their characters without me playing god over their shoulders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T12:17:59-07:00","id":1484717,"title":"","content":"It's also possible to make a case that Dracula was specifically weak against the symbols of Catholic faith rather than Stoker claiming that Catholicism is objectively true (at least not in conscious way on the author's behalf). Stoker's fictionalized version of Vlad Tepes was specifically a traitor to the Roman Catholic church, not just a general blasphemous person.<br /> <br /> More importantly a novel isn't an interactive RPG. A novel author exploring the emotional reaction to the idea that a monster only responds to the holy symbols of a specific sect of a specific religion is not that same experience as a RPG that declares a specific sect of a specific religion holds the objective truth of the game's setting; esp. if that's actively enforced in the rules. There's nothing interesting to actually play for narrative and dramatic effect if we all know who's right and who's wrong before anything happens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T16:39:05-07:00","id":1484729,"title":"","content":"The good thing about CoD's 2nd ed systems is precisely that they're not ultimately linked to morality. It's a subtle distinction that makes a huge difference in contextualizing what your rolls and eventual loss means. They're about your ability to cope with your condition and remain functional in society (yours or mortal). Each &quot;Integrity&quot; trait works differently because what it means to become dysfunctional will change for each splat.<br /> <br /> For normal humans, it is coping with Trauma, for Vampires it is being able to pass as Human, which is a very nice twist. No more having a high Humanity score means being a good person, or believing you're entitled to be a monster means you need to abandon Humanity. You can believe in your own goodness and strive to be good even at a low score, and you can be a despicable monster and still want high Humanity to be a wolf in sheep's clothes.<br /> <br /> Otherwise Morality will inevitably fall in this same place again and again. It may be fun for some people to just be able to reinforce on most chronicles that their own faith is objectively true, and now and then change things for kicks. But for someone that has to constantly deal with obnoxious claims to absolute morality irl, using religion to demonize others, to justify their prejudices and to deny others their own merits and say that good morals actually only come from their god, facing this kind of absolutism in a game is abhorrent.<br /> <br /> Now, with how the game actually developed with Paths and Roads, this use of several Morality Systems to try to curb the Beast is also a very interesting option that acquired its own history in the setting, and I think that has some value. In this, I agree that the best for VtM may not be to just apply VtR Humanity, but instead use DAV Roads. And then you can even keep the idea of Humanity becoming a default due to the rise of Humanism as a common moral background in the last centuries, which would make it less an objective moral system and more of a sign of the times.<br /> <br /> Mechanically I think the V5 system has a better potential than the strict Hierarchy from previous editions, but for now the Roads work better, V5's Humanity still needs a lot of polishing (and maybe becoming even more Road-like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T19:57:42-07:00","id":1484747,"title":"","content":"I like how Humanity as done and while Roads are fascinating to read about in my limited experience they were more of &quot;just another topic for the GM to keep in mind while doing his work&quot; than anything that was adding as much to the game as it did work. But that's just my experience with them.<br /> <br /> But to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T22:03:10-07:00","id":1484755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484747#post1484747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how Humanity as done and while Roads are fascinating to read about in my limited experience they were more of &quot;just another topic for the GM to keep in mind while doing his work&quot; than anything that was adding as much to the game as it did work. But that's just my experience with them.<br /> <br /> But to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Experience plays a lot into it, but you don't really need much to apply the main gist of it:<ul><li>Keep in mind that Humanity isn't the only way, although it is the default and more common way;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>You don't need to understand every Path, only the Path you'll use, from the perspective of the actual character;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>The regular Path Follower isn't either a shiny paragon of the Path nor a knowledgeable sage of its philosophy;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>If a player wants to follow a Path, let them do the hard work for you in researching and explaining it, then check;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Paths are complex, but it just means that followers also make mistakes and disagree, feel free to make mistakes;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Just keep in mind they exist, really. As background element they'll help you a lot without any need for exploration.<br /> \u200b</li> </ul><br /> This kind of work is manageable when you get the trick of simply not trying to grasp it all at once. We have a tendency to assume that we need to understand something comprehensively to apply it on our games, but actually just throwing in bits and pieces as they get interesting to use goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T11:51:13-07:00","id":1484787,"title":"","content":"My biggest problem with humanity in a vampire game is that the threat of losing it all is for the character to become a mindless (and uninteresting) NPC monster, that is if you lose it all. I've always felt that it would be much better to instead give other kind of changes to characters as they lose their humanity, like giving them derangments and mental flaws, perhaps even physical flaws, things that could make the story more interesting in showing the character's fall. I never really liked the idea of wassail, it never felt really engaging or interesting and as such they're very rare in most games...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-23-2022, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:56:21-07:00","id":1484797,"title":"","content":"Possibly gaining derangements from losing Humanity was a think for all of VtM 1e to V20, and was in VtR 1e as well.<br /> <br /> Having Humanity zero being a fail state (like a character dying) is something worth considering how effective it is, but even if you want characters to be able to recover from Humanity 0, it needs to be a severe enough condition that PCs are rightfully scared of it rather than it being inconvenient. It shouldn't be a ditch that you accidentally fall into and then have to deal with the relatively minor hassle of pulling yourself up.<br /> <br /> While there's a lot of reasons people ignore Beast: the Primordial from the CofD, it's Integrity trait (Satiety) is actually a really good model for alternatives to the Humanity approach. Hitting Satiety 0 is something you can recover from, and it's a fairly pressing issue because you're dying slowly while you're there. But it takes a considerable effort to do, and you're stuck without access to a lot of things that would help considerably as Satiety is also your fuel for a lot of your powers. It's an &quot;Oh Shit!&quot; moment to be stuck spending your last Satiety, because it's still really serious even if not instantly lose your character so.<br /> <br /> It's also worth considering that if you keep Humanity linked to morality, the whole &quot;gain a derangement&quot; thing is actually really... not cool. That's why CofD 2e stopped that It's important to separate out doing &quot;immoral&quot; things from causing real world psychological conditions in people. You can keep some level of this (doing immortal things is frequently traumatic, and trauma has clear mental health concerns), but you need to be pretty careful with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:12:59-07:00","id":1484801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484787#post1484787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest problem with humanity in a vampire game is that the threat of losing it all is for the character to become a mindless (and uninteresting) NPC monster, that is if you lose it all. I've always felt that it would be much more better to instead give other kind of changes to characters as they lose their humanity, like giving them derangments and mental flaws, perhaps even physical flaws, things that could make the story more interesting in showing the character's fall. I never really liked the idea of wassail, it never felt really engaging or interesting and as such they're very rare in most games...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the basic idea always seemed to be that a vampire's ultimate fate was to become like Lucy in Dracula, and like the vampires in Salem's Lot: creatures who feel nothing but a desire for blood, and whose intelligence can only be focused on extremely crude manipulations. The corpse floating outside your window saying clumsily manipulative things to get an invitation while it's face makes it clear that it is totally focused on drinking you dry and has not a shred of emotional depth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T15:35:19-07:00","id":1484809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484787#post1484787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest problem with humanity in a vampire game is that the threat of losing it all is for the character to become a mindless (and uninteresting) NPC monster, that is if you lose it all. I've always felt that it would be much more better to instead give other kind of changes to characters as they lose their humanity, like giving them derangments and mental flaws, perhaps even physical flaws, things that could make the story more interesting in showing the character's fall. I never really liked the idea of wassail, it never felt really engaging or interesting and as such they're very rare in most games...</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest, if you want to go in that way, to create a special state when a character fall to humanity 0.<br /> The condition are up to the ST but when a character lose all humanity he has a (really small) chance to change into a pure evil being, but keep his mental ability<br /> You can imagine a Vampire so evil that he would do absolutly everything he want, like a dark version of golconda. You can describe that kind of character like a Devil coming straight from hell to destroy or dominate everything.<br /> <br /> That kind of absolute monster could be a perfect main antagonist for a story, or a fallen companion who has lost so much that he succumbed to hatred until he became one with the beast. And in that state he could diablerise without fearing to lost anything, he's already lost. In addition as the character would keep his mind a player could still play it and have fun becoming a terrific monster<br /> <br /> Just an idea that i found interesting to share","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-23-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:04:19-07:00","id":1484812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> want characters to be able to recover from Humanity 0, it needs to be a severe enough condition that PCs are rightfully scared of it rather than it being inconvenient. </div> </div> </div>I feel that the problem is that it's way too radical in not giving them any chance of recover. By the way, wights were never really well explored in the game, so the thought is always that the character becomes a &quot;stupid NPC monster&quot;. Another thing that is linked to that is how intelligent the beast is, many interpret it as a completely mindless &quot;thing&quot;, so that if, for instance, a blood mage becomes a wight or even just in frenzy, he stops being a threat, because the beast isn't able to use cast blood magic. The books never explored it well enough or gave us a picture of what a character in frenzy is able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the whole &quot;gain a derangement&quot; thing is actually really... not cool. </div> </div> </div>It's what happens to mortals by the rules, when their humanity would fall to 0, they instead gain a derangement and the humanity keeps at 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The corpse floating outside your window saying clumsily manipulative things to get an invitation while it's face makes it clear that it is totally focused on drinking you dry and has not a shred of emotional depth. </div> </div> </div>You made it look interesting there, I know this is what is supposed to happen, but what are the limits of what such a character can do and what can such a character make to redeem himself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The condition are up to the ST but when a character lose all humanity he has a (really small) chance to change into a pure evil being, but keep his mental ability<br /> You can imagine a Vampire so evil that he would do absolutly everything he want, like a dark version of golconda. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea, I'm in fact concerned with the limits of what a character dominated by the beast is able to do in terms of thinking, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:12:46-07:00","id":1484814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484812#post1484812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You made it look interesting there, I know this is what is supposed to happen, but what are the limits of what such a character can do and what can such a character make to redeem himself?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to base its limits off the sort of fiction that inspired it. Wights are based off creatures who retain their human intelligence, but become so emotionally simple that they are only capable of crude short-term manipulations and short-term tactical thinking. Crude use of Presence and Dominate. Stripping and rubbing themselves lasciviously to get an invitation. Calling a friend on the phone and asking if they can come over, while not really being able to hide the hunger and glee in their voice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:18:58-07:00","id":1484817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484814#post1484814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would tend to base its limits off the sort of fiction that inspired it. Wights are based off creatures who retain their human intelligence, but become so emotionally simple that they are only capable of crude short-term manipulations and short-term tactical thinking. Crude use of Presence and Dominate. Stripping and rubbing themselves lasciviously to get an invitation. Calling a friend on the phone and asking if they can come over, while not really being able to hide the hunger and glee in their voice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But would you think they can cast blood magic? That's always being a hot topic among my friends, because it's never really determined by the books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:26:48-07:00","id":1484819,"title":"","content":"I would think yes, though only when the benefit would be obvious to someone whose thoughts are very short-term tactical, not at all strategic. Wights aren't stupid, just so emotionally simple that their ability to channel their intelligence is limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:28:13-07:00","id":1484820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484817#post1484817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But would you think they can cast blood magic? That's always being a hot topic among my friends, because it's never really determined by the books...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Wight\" target=\"_blank\">wiki</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As Wights are purely Beasts with no Man to guide them, and as such they rarely can use a Discipline over level three, and cannot use Disciplines that require finesse, patience, or ritual behavior. Physical disciplines (Potence, Fortitude, Celerity) have no upper limits except the maximum dictated by the Wight\u2019s generation, but all forms of blood magic (both paths and rituals) are unusable by wights.<br /> Being incapable of any form of social interaction other than that which intimidates or causes fear, Dominate is inaccessible to them, such as most powers of Presence (for instance, they can use Dread Gaze, but not Awe). A Wight developing Obfuscate would learn only the first two levels, as the third is too involved for its mind to grasp. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:01:02-07:00","id":1484824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484787#post1484787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest problem with humanity in a vampire game is that the threat of losing it all is for the character to become a mindless (and uninteresting) NPC monster,</div> </div> </div> </div>The threat of losing all of your Humanity is a problem since always.<br /> <br /> If the vampire gets simpler and simpler in emotions as it sinks to the Beast, why would it even go to the extremes of perversion needed to lose the last dot? I mean, has anyone ever seen in play a character, even NPC, lose the last point of Humanity to something other than Diablerie? Has anyone seen a character even sink that low without doing so on purpose (like to change Paths)?<br /> <br /> But yeah, it needs also a different set of teeth, that just hasn't ever been a big problem because losing it all is so damn hard to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:10:19-07:00","id":1484825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484812#post1484812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that the problem is that it's way too radical in not giving them any chance of recover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The chance to recover is buying dots in your Humanity/Path rating before letting it fall to zero. If a character takes too much damage, they die without any chance for medical or supernatural healing. The chance to avoid that was everything before they got hit for that much damage compared to their current health. It's not like you can drop from Humanity 5 to 0 in one roll, you need to do some pretty serious nasty stuff to fall to zero.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying being a wight has to be final like that, but I think you're overstating things because of how much it takes in the current rules (V20 or V5) to get there. Recovering from being a wight shouldn't be a light task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...for instance, a blood mage becomes a wight or even just in frenzy, he stops being a threat, because the beast isn't able to use cast blood magic. </div> </div> </div>Less of a threat doesn't make them not a threat. While they can no longer activate blood magic, any active long duration effects they've cast on them are still there, and any other powers they might have access too. Plus all the powers of being a vampire they still have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's what happens to mortals by the rules, when their humanity would fall to 0, they instead gain a derangement and the humanity keeps at 1. </div> </div> </div>Still bad. CofD 1e Morality (which Integrity replaced) also gave mortals derangements too. The problem is that a lot of people struggling with mental health issues really hated the whole &quot;immortality = disorders,&quot; mindset behind it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:57:38-07:00","id":1484829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484825#post1484825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still bad. CofD 1e Morality (which Integrity replaced) also gave mortals derangements too. The problem is that a lot of people struggling with mental health issues really hated the whole &quot;immortality = disorders,&quot; mindset behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. There's a lot of problems in linking even Integrity loss to Derangement, doing so with Humanity has even more issues.<br /> <br /> There are <i>some</i> links that make sense. For example, killing a person is extremely traumatic (historically, despite all the violence, very few soldiers through history really could move themselves to a killing blow with any regularity, and most battle-related deaths were from complications from wounds), which is one of the things that result in many soldiers and cops dealing with nasty cases of PTSD, it's the combination of what they went through with what they did.<br /> <br /> But even this is extremely complicated to really put in a game and too prone to cause bad reactions instead of offering a sensible representation of the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T19:35:44-07:00","id":1484834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Recovering from being a wight shouldn't be a light task. </div> </div> </div>Certainly not, that's not what I meant at all. I just think there should be a way stated in the books, etc. Perhaps that could be the goal of an entire story arc, etc. I just don't like the idea of it being permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T19:37:34-07:00","id":1484835,"title":"","content":"Also, I don't think diablerie should ALWAYS make your humanity drop, I mean if you amaranth a very bad guy just to make better use of his powers, for instance, etc. It's not that impossible to find justifications for diablerie to make it sounds less terrible, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:24:13-07:00","id":1484840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484835#post1484835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't think diablerie should ALWAYS make your humanity drop, I mean if you amaranth a very bad guy just to make better use of his powers, for instance, etc. It's not that impossible to find justifications for diablerie to make it sounds less terrible, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should vary based on chronicle tenets. Really, all the &quot;Always Cause Stains&quot; stuff should also only cause stains based off tenets, as well. It feels like diablerie and the always causes stains stuff assumes you take Humanistic tenets or close to it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T21:35:59-07:00","id":1484841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484835#post1484835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't think diablerie should ALWAYS make your humanity drop, I mean if you amaranth a very bad guy just to make better use of his powers, for instance, etc. It's not that impossible to find justifications for diablerie to make it sounds less terrible, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make the argument, &quot;What if it happened to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Would <b>you</b> want to be eaten and then forcibly absorbed by some power-hungry asshole?<br /> <br /> Unlike executing a horrific monster, which can be justified, diablerie carries much more risks then just killing them. First, you're eating their soul, which is worse than killing as it guarantees that <b>if</b> there is an afterlife in WoD, other than the shadowlands, then they won't see it. Not only that, but it also opens you to being possessed by said monster.<br /> <br /> I hate using Hitler, because it's too easy, but what if you ate vampire Hitler? What if you lost the spiritual fight against vampire Hitler? Vampire Hitler is not only still active but is in a better position since everyone thinks he's dead. Even then, you now have a piece of vampire Hitler inside of you. A piece that has fused with you and has caused a subtle change you will never notice.<br /> <br /> That is what Diablerie is, the absorption of someone else into you. If they were good, you just killed an innocent person and guaranteed they'd never come back. If they were a piece of shit, that piece of shit has been taken into you and you are now a little bit more a piece of shit. Either way you slice it, Diablerie should have a humanity drop IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T22:05:44-07:00","id":1484844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484841#post1484841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd make the argument, &quot;What if it happened to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Would <b>you</b> want to be eaten and then forcibly absorbed by some power-hungry asshole?<br /> <br /> Unlike executing a horrific monster, which can be justified, diablerie carries much more risks then just killing them. First, you're eating their soul, which is worse than killing as it guarantees that <b>if</b> there is an afterlife in WoD, other than the shadowlands, then they won't see it. Not only that, but it also opens you to being possessed by said monster.<br /> <br /> I hate using Hitler, because it's too easy, but what if you ate vampire Hitler? What if you lost the spiritual fight against vampire Hitler? Vampire Hitler is not only still active but is in a better position since everyone thinks he's dead. Even then, you now have a piece of vampire Hitler inside of you. A piece that has fused with you and has caused a subtle change you will never notice.<br /> <br /> That is what Diablerie is, the absorption of someone else into you. If they were good, you just killed an innocent person and guaranteed they'd never come back. If they were a piece of shit, that piece of shit has been taken into you and you are now a little bit more a piece of shit. Either way you slice it, Diablerie should have a humanity drop IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could be justifiable in some very specific cases, not that it's irrelevant. Of course it's in general very bad, but perhaps for a giving story it wouldn't carry such terrible consequences like potentially dropping humanity to 0, that's what I think is too much. Perhaps it could be a sin until humanity 2 or so. Imagine a story based on the highlander concept, in such a story it could be argued that it's not that bad. Also, the fact that you can be possessed by the enemy is even more interesting, as it's the risk and we need diablerie to have its risks as well as its benefits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it should vary based on chronicle tenets. Really, all the &quot;Always Cause Stains&quot; stuff should also only cause stains based off tenets, as well. It feels like diablerie and the always causes stains stuff assumes you take Humanistic tenets or close to it. </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I think, I think it should always be based on the story being told, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T23:27:43-07:00","id":1484845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484841#post1484841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you're eating their soul, which is worse than killing as it guarantees that <b>if</b> there is an afterlife in WoD, other than the shadowlands, then they won't see it. Not only that, but it also opens you to being possessed by said monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you're <b><u>supposedly</u></b> eating their soul.<br /> <br /> What if the one doing it simply does not believe that to be the case?<br /> <br /> You also <b><u>supposedly</u></b> run the risk of possession, but considering that a) the text makes it very clear that this is an extremely unlikely outcome even when devouring the power of an extremely ancient vampire (being partially affected by their memories/personality is far more common and already rare), and b) it also says directly that most characters are unaware of such risk, this is both too low and too unlikely to have moral weight in the action.<br /> <br /> The discussion is not about the effects of Diablerie, but about its impact on Humanity and what it says about Humanity. Do you mean by this that there's an objective, non-personal morality, this morality will get to you even if you're unaware of the &quot;correct&quot; interpretation of your actions, even with this interpretation not necessarily being correct as a phenomenon, just as moral grounds for losing your sense of self?<br /> <br /> And what if Diablerie is the only way to be sure that your opponent will be completely destroyed? So many vampires have so many means to fake their deaths and flee. Diablerie can give a sense of security in the deed that may actually be absolutely necessary for the task at hand.<br /> <br /> If we run with the &quot;Classic&quot; Humanity/Roads system, we have the advantage that no moral code need to be &quot;true&quot; to work, as long as it is sufficiently ingrained (which is the reason why merely believing you're in the right does not make you &quot;feel&quot; right, and feeling is paramount to the process), but then Diablerie being inescapable doesn't really make sense. If we run with Requiem 2nd Humanity we have the advantage that it isn't about morals to begin with, and then we can examine the effects through another lens and have the same result with completely distinct meanings for the fiction, but that also means dropping the moral side of the equation completely.<br /> <br /> Humanity 0 being permanent is its own can of worms. Things get more confusing when you consider that even the authors (or some of them) agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> at least to an extent: Kemintiri is an example of a character that supposedly came back from there with the help of Bardo, and this story has some consistency. That would make at least one known way back from Wassail. But I think that for now it is simply too hard to even get there to worry so much with the come back process, like too hard even if you try, and you hardly have any reason to try.<br /> <br /> Just stationing at Humanity 1 or 2 is too easy even for the most depraved vampire, unless Diablerie Rules fuck them, and as long as we have this little problem, being able to bounce back becomes an afterthought. For now there are only two ways to go that low that are likely to affect a PC, or to get even an NPC unaware: failing at changing Paths or getting addicted to Diablerie. Even then both are hard to end that badly in practice. Without other motivations to get there, there are few stories to be told about the downfall to Wassail, and no need to come back from something you won't get into.<br /> <br /> Requiem solved this partially with two additional Rank 1 Breaking Points, but keeping in mind that Humanity in Requiem, again, is more about sense of self and ability to function among the sheep than being a moral person. You risk the last dot if you go 10 years without any human contact or if you kill your Touchstone yourself, even by accident (Touchstones in Requiem have less downsides, more and better benefits and are far easier to replace, even expected to be so no matter your age). This makes the risk of losing it far more palpable, something you can succumb to by accident, intervention of your enemies, or even trying to do good, yet still so hard that you won't find yourself at the end of the line just by dumb luck, but you certainly have to keep on your toes about where your Humanity is going to. It has also far smarter Draugr, the Humanity 0 vampires that still follow the concept <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> gave, but can even fool the other vampires in believing they're still functional if not pressed hard (hunting Draugr is a far more pressing matter in Requiem).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T02:36:54-07:00","id":1484853,"title":"","content":"One way to better define why you lose humanity is to understand what is the beast and what is his influence.<br /> As described the beast is an instinct of pure destruction, the animality of the vampire that devour him with time. <br /> <br /> So why are you losing humanity? When tou awake the beast or accept his influence you let it take over, so you become more a monster. But it also feed on you when you let your guard down, when you're feeling shame, sadness or whatever emotional combination that weakens your mind and allow the beast to force his grip on the character.<br /> <br /> So the beast grow stronger when you let it or when you're mind is too weaken to resist<br /> What can weaken your mind? Well this is where it get difficult, because it depend on the person: a soldier would better accept killing when it's self defense or for a very good reason but a doctor will never accept that. <br /> Humanity as described in the game is a generic system for the character, but the same way there's path of enlightment there's different morality, and therefore humanity depending on the person<br /> So basicaly if you want to make humanity working the way you want in your game you must define a clear moral code for each of the players:<br /> A soldier would accept killing (no roll or at lower difficulty) while a doctor would not accept it unless getting really low in his humanity<br /> In addition it bring mixity in the different way of playing, the players can complete the other when one can do something the others cannot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-24-2022, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T03:29:58-07:00","id":1484855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484608#post1484608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, VtM Paths are stupid.&quot;I wanna avoid turning into a mindless monsters, so I'll conciously turn into a mindful one&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You just described humanity and pretty much all the personal horror aspects of vtm there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T03:46:04-07:00","id":1484856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484824#post1484824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The threat of losing all of your Humanity is a problem since always.<br /> <br /> If the vampire gets simpler and simpler in emotions as it sinks to the Beast, why would it even go to the extremes of perversion needed to lose the last dot? I mean, has anyone ever seen in play a character, even NPC, lose the last point of Humanity to something other than Diablerie? Has anyone seen a character even sink that low without doing so on purpose (like to change Paths)?<br /> <br /> But yeah, it needs also a different set of teeth, that just hasn't ever been a big problem because losing it all is so damn hard to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw a player botch their path jump role and oddly enough I had someone a metamorphosis wassail because she couldn't let go of her national pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T05:11:47-07:00","id":1484859,"title":"","content":"Well, there is a third, or maybe a 2.5 option to that list: Vampires that lose their last dot of Humanity because a Path vampire is trying to indoctrinate them and pushes them too far.<br /> <br /> Losing that last few dots of Humanity pre-V5 depends a lot on how the ST treats the Beast and Frenzies. As you drop to low Humanity, you lose dice to resist Frenzy, making them more common. If you have to roll degeneration checks for actions taken during such Frenzies, and the Beast pushes your PC into the horrific acts necessary for low Humanity loss, the possibility does grow significantly compared to either or both of those interpretations being treated differently.<br /> <br /> It's not a particularly fun thing, because it's basically waiting for the ST to screw you and take your character away, but it is a possibility in how one might play the game.<br /> <br /> Again, I think VtR 2e does this better. There are Humanity checks that you run the risk of over time even at Humanity 1. You can never be truly safe there, even without the ST needing to hijack your PC during a Frenzy to make you do horrific things. Diablerie addiction in VtR 2e is probably one of the surest ways to eventually drop to Humanity zero because while VtR 2e don't make it automatic Humanity loss, it's always a check, and a lot of the ways to help get bonuses to detachment breaking points are reduced or lost at low Humanity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T08:05:24-07:00","id":1484869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484855#post1484855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just described humanity and pretty much all the personal horror aspects of vtm there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt call it exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T08:21:07-07:00","id":1484871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484869#post1484869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldnt call it exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. &quot;A beast I am lest a beast I become.&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T08:35:14-07:00","id":1484874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484871#post1484871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would. &amp;quot;A beast I am lest a beast I become.&amp;quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a nice slogan and all but it isnt part of the personal horror in Vampire, which is your slow decay and detachment from your human condition, eventually turning into a inhuman monster.<br /> <br /> The Paths however bypass that and instead allows you to simply glorify and bask on evil for the sake of evil. I mean, why would the &quot;threat of the beast&quot; ever be a threat at all if your morality glorifies psychopatic behavior? The beast just becomes stupidity if all you have to do and be is a self servient psychopath that cares only about yourself and your own survival - and such paths become perfect tools of survival that you'll always strive to advance into.<br /> <br /> Also, if you turn into a self servient psychopath, you already discarded your human self entirely; that should be the definition of the Beast, not it's polar opposite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T08:48:54-07:00","id":1484875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484874#post1484874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's a nice slogan and all but it isnt part of the personal horror in Vampire, which is your slow decay and detachment from your human condition, eventually turning into a inhuman monster.<br /> <br /> The Paths however bypass that and instead allows you to simply glorify and bask on evil for the sake of evil. I mean, why would the &quot;threat of the beast&quot; ever be a threat at all if your morality glorifies psychopatic behavior? The beast just becomes stupidity if all you have to do and be is a self servient psychopath that cares only about yourself and your own survival - and such paths become perfect tools of survival that you'll always strive to advance into.<br /> <br /> Also, if you turn into a self servient psychopath, you already discarded your human self entirely; that should be the definition of the Beast, not it's polar opposite</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not merely a slogan its the games design philosophy. Pretty much yeah so ultimatly post early vampires the distinction between a path and humanity becomes redundant, you do horrible things and rationalise them.<br /> <br /> Not really paths tend to be quote morally complex in terms of philosophy and 'good' with their own unique restraints and obligations. The beast remains a threat to both your ideals and sense of self if you're on a path.<br /> <br /> No even if that where true an psychopath is nothing like the beast. Psychopaths still have concepts such as sense of self, abstract thinking and Higher reasoning and all that this entails. A psychopath would most likely hate and fear the beasts when they correctly realised its an existential threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T09:49:41-07:00","id":1484878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484875#post1484875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not merely a slogan its the games design philosophy. Pretty much yeah so ultimatly post early vampires the distinction between a path and humanity becomes redundant, you do horrible things and rationalise them.<br /> <br /> Not really paths tend to be quote morally complex in terms of philosophy and 'good' with their own unique restraints and obligations. The beast remains a threat to both your ideals and sense of self if you're on a path.<br /> <br /> No even if that where true an psychopath is nothing like the beast. Psychopaths still have concepts such as sense of self, abstract thinking and Higher reasoning and all that this entails. A psychopath would most likely hate and fear the beasts when they correctly realised its an existential threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Beast is NOT an existential threat to someone that has already psychopathic morals! That's the thing. About &quot;rationalizing&quot; yes, a Humanity 2 vampire is a monster that can rationalize a lot of stuff - but no matter how detached, there's still a few limits and if you cross those, at humanity 2 you're dangetously close to the Beast.<br /> <br /> What's the threat of the Beast for someone with 10 in &quot;Evil Revelations&quot;? Woahahaha, Im a big monster, a fiend from hell who is bound to spread evil (for evil's sake, mind you). Woahahaha, look at my awesome evilness! And the more evil, the less bestial I am! I just need to avoid doing good deeds without some bigger evil behind them which will be suuuuuuper hard for my demonic personality to do but hey, such is life, I'll resist the temptation, this &quot;urge&quot; to do good that boils in my soul...<br /> <br /> I mean... Comon, let us be real here. Half of those paths were ridiculous, and the other half were absurd.<br /> <br /> And lastly, for vampires with low humanity, you rationalize your actions because you are CLOSER to the Beast.<br /> <br /> While the Paths have you rationalize your actions because you are FARTHER away from the Beast; it doesnt make any sense this. <br /> <br /> What's the personal horror if turning into an inhuman monster is GOOD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T12:19:08-07:00","id":1484887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Paths however bypass that and instead allows you to simply glorify and bask on evil for the sake of evil. I mean, why would the &quot;threat of the beast&quot; ever be a threat at all if your morality glorifies psychopatic behavior? </div> </div> </div>Talk about oversimplification... you're treating all paths as if they were Path of Evil Revelations, when it's clearly a niche path for infernalists and heavily advertised to not be used by PCs. Most Paths stems from philosophical views of life and are in many cases much harder to follow than humanity itself, just with different, but yet hard to follow, moral codes. You're merely oversimplifying them as if they were all &quot;Path of Evil Revelations&quot; when this path is clearly designed to one of the most virulent forms of infernalism in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T12:59:36-07:00","id":1484889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484755#post1484755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Experience plays a lot into it, but you don't really need much to apply the main gist of it:<ul><li>Keep in mind that Humanity isn't the only way, although it is the default and more common way;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>You don't need to understand every Path, only the Path you'll use, from the perspective of the actual character;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>The regular Path Follower isn't either a shiny paragon of the Path nor a knowledgeable sage of its philosophy;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>If a player wants to follow a Path, let them do the hard work for you in researching and explaining it, then check;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Paths are complex, but it just means that followers also make mistakes and disagree, feel free to make mistakes;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Just keep in mind they exist, really. As background element they'll help you a lot without any need for exploration.<br /> \u200b</li> </ul><br /> <br /> This kind of work is manageable when you get the trick of simply not trying to grasp it all at once. We have a tendency to assume that we need to understand something comprehensively to apply it on our games, but actually just throwing in bits and pieces as they get interesting to use goes a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I think that I wrote. To each their own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T16:01:01-07:00","id":1484902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484878#post1484878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the Beast is NOT an existential threat to someone that has already psychopathic morals! That's the thing. About &quot;rationalizing&quot; yes, a Humanity 2 vampire is a monster that can rationalize a lot of stuff - but no matter how detached, there's still a few limits and if you cross those, at humanity 2 you're dangetously close to the Beast.<br /> <br /> What's the threat of the Beast for someone with 10 in &quot;Evil Revelations&quot;? Woahahaha, Im a big monster, a fiend from hell who is bound to spread evil (for evil's sake, mind you). Woahahaha, look at my awesome evilness! And the more evil, the less bestial I am! I just need to avoid doing good deeds without some bigger evil behind them which will be suuuuuuper hard for my demonic personality to do but hey, such is life, I'll resist the temptation, this &quot;urge&quot; to do good that boils in my soul...<br /> <br /> I mean... Comon, let us be real here. Half of those paths were ridiculous, and the other half were absurd.<br /> <br /> And lastly, for vampires with low humanity, you rationalize your actions because you are CLOSER to the Beast.<br /> <br /> While the Paths have you rationalize your actions because you are FARTHER away from the Beast; it doesnt make any sense this. <br /> <br /> What's the personal horror if turning into an inhuman monster is GOOD?</div> </div> </div> </div>It must certainly is paths have strict rules and are quite easy to slip into breaching. Agreed and low path members have the same peril<br /> <br /> Aside from eternal damnation and a cross sect death sentence? Revelations is actually very restrictive you have to consistantly act as en extension of Evil even if it's a terrible idea at the moment or even contrary to your survival. You cannot any engage in altruistic action-consider how restrictive and destructive that'd be irl.<br /> <br /> I'll conceed they're genrally not Kant with fangs but you're severly underselling them the rationale and mindsets of each path are explained and reasoned to the perspectives mindset.<br /> <br /> Yes but im not talking about degeneration rolls I'm talking about the endless rationalising of being a vampire full stop.The average humanity vampire has to hold on to extensive list of rationalising beyond degeneration rolls.....like paths you lie to yourself that you shouldnt just wait for sunrise.<br /> <br /> The absolute desolation of who you've become and all that entails while burning out your decency doesn't strike you as horrific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-24-2022, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T17:01:54-07:00","id":1484908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484902#post1484902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The absolute desolation of who you've become and all that entails while burning out your decency doesn't strike you as horrific?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's horrific for me because Im a non-psycopathic human being.<br /> <br /> This idea however is not horrific for a vampire that decided to embrace any such paths, be it Evil Revelations, Paradox or any such. To them it is good to be evil, they dont revile in that notion, they bask on it.<br /> <br /> A Humanity 2 vampire may look at himself and realize that he's a monster, and ponder about how far he has felt. A vamp following the Paradox Path that reaches 10 in the Path would feel proud of how &quot;enlightned&quot; he is, and would feel joy in how inhuman he has become. That's not personal terror, that's silly. That's like playing a merry demon that feels delighted in being evil.<br /> <br /> And Evil Revelations is an extreme case oviously, but there are many other paths that are just as evil but arent as reviled by the Kindred society and doesnt mean being hunted down, and that just as equally glorifies their inhuman monstruosity.<br /> <br /> The idea about the Humanity has always being about getting detached from your human condition, and slowly turn into a monster; that's the personal horror of it.<br /> <br /> If instead you become a happy monster, that's no longer a personal horror game, it just becomes a game of gore brutality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T17:02:49-07:00","id":1484909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484856#post1484856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw a player botch their path jump role and oddly enough I had someone a metamorphosis wassail because she couldn't let go of her national pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which brings us to one of the most ironic effects of the actual rules in the classic system: Paths were created to help you keep the Beast at bay while becoming a monster, but it is actually safer to just stick to Humanity, because that last dot is so damn hard to lose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484878#post1484878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Beast is NOT an existential threat to someone that has already psychopathic morals!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very wrong notion of what Psychopathy means and a narrow notion of what an existential threat the Beast represents.<br /> <br /> Humanity is a moral code working as a buffer against the Beast, but it is not the opposite of the Beast any more than plexiglass is the opposite of lead just because it's used to make bulletproof riot shields.<br /> <br /> What the Beast entails isn't a lack of morality, but the death of your sense of self. It is to have your dreams, goals, ambitions, desires, memories, everything utterly destroyed to become an entity whose mind is limited to that of a Romero zombie or even less. That's not something someone would want to become just because they're amoral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484878#post1484878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the threat of the Beast for someone with 10 in &quot;Evil Revelations&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to analyze each Path from &quot;bottom to top&quot;, as the lower rungs are the most basic principles, the things that are utter perversions to a follower and can lead them not just to a loss, but to Wassail. The higher sins are only relevant for Path &quot;saints&quot; that avoid all 10 of them.<br /> <br /> The very first sin of <b>Evil Revelations</b> is to disobey the master. So you'll go all the way to Wassail if you don't have complete obedience to an NPC that has no regard to your well being and no reason to be nice to you whatsoever. The second sin declares that even being neutral to another vampire is unacceptable, you have to be constantly (if subtly) trying to convert or destroy everyone around you. You can take your time, but if someone escapes, this is a freaking level 2 sin. Go up from there and many sins will require actions that have a very considerable chance of jeopardizing your plans, ambitions and even survival, and even things that can come to bite your ass without any fault of your own (you were tricked or forced with Dominate into revealing some infernal secrets, even minor ones that you can easily brush as something you read in a book? Level 3 sin, son).<br /> <br /> I used to think the same, but as I started to actually pay attention I realized that many Paths are really hard to follow in actual play, and really are things a character would follow only because they're zealots. I'd say Humanity is actually one of the easiest, specially at the lower steps, those that can really screw you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T17:13:31-07:00","id":1484912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484908#post1484908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's horrific for me because Im a non-psycopathic human being.<br /> <br /> This idea however is not horrific for a vampire that decided to embrace any such paths, be it Evil Revelations, Paradox or any such. To them it is good to be evil, they dont revile in that notion, they bask on it.<br /> <br /> A Humanity 2 vampire may look at himself and realize that he's a monster, and ponder about how far he has felt. A vamp following the Paradox Path that reaches 10 in the Path would feel proud of how &quot;enlightned&quot; he is, and would feel joy in how inhuman he has become. That's not personal terror, that's silly. That's like playing a merry demon that feels delighted in being evil.<br /> <br /> And Evil Revelations is an extreme case oviously, but there are many other paths that are just as evil but arent as reviled by the Kindred society and doesnt mean being hunted down, and that just as equally glorifies their inhuman monstruosity.<br /> <br /> The idea about the Humanity has always being about getting detached from your human condition, and slowly turn into a monster; that's the personal horror of it.<br /> <br /> If instead you become a happy monster, that's no longer a personal horror game, it just becomes a game of gore brutality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes which would be enough on its own.<br /> <br /> You sure? Exactly how a vampire reacts to path membership is pretty complex.<br /> <br /> Possibly alternatively he might be so beast addled he's barely sapient.<br /> <br /> No it aspires to inhumanity its an important distinction.<br /> <br /> And an obvious extension of that dillema is how and when you accept a degree of monstrosity to maintain a sense of self. Also that's pretty a early game approach. If you're over about 10 years you've already cultivated a degree of monstrosity path or no.<br /> <br /> That's the catch-typically their not 'happy' monsters They're typically more vader than palpatine. Especially ar 1-4 on their paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-24-2022, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T18:01:28-07:00","id":1484916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484912#post1484912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes which would be enough on its own.<br /> <br /> You sure? Exactly how a vampire reacts to path membership is pretty complex.<br /> <br /> Possibly alternatively he might be so beast addled he's barely sapient.<br /> <br /> No it aspires to inhumanity its an important distinction.<br /> <br /> And an obvious extension of that dillema is how and when you accept a degree of monstrosity to maintain a sense of self. Also that's pretty a early game approach. If you're over about 10 years you've already cultivated a degree of monstrosity path or no.<br /> <br /> That's the catch-typically their not 'happy' monsters They're typically more vader than palpatine. Especially ar 1-4 on their paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, lets agree to disagree then. We obviously have different perspectives on this subject; I think it's about how we view the path towards the Beast or rather saying what the Beast represents, more than the implications of morality itself, so I dont think we can convince one another either way. Im not sure either view is wrong thou, not mine but also neither is yours, now that Im beggining to understand it; so perhaps what needed clarifying was exactly what the Beast is by the part of the writers. And if they were to say that indeed it is how you believe it to be, I would have to say that it doesnt please me a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T08:08:49-07:00","id":1485374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484541-humanity-and-morality-opinions-wanted?p=1484908#post1484908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's horrific for me because Im a non-psycopathic human being.<br /> <br /> This idea however is not horrific for a vampire that decided to embrace any such paths, be it Evil Revelations, Paradox or any such. To them it is good to be evil, they dont revile in that notion, they bask on it.<br /> <br /> A Humanity 2 vampire may look at himself and realize that he's a monster, and ponder about how far he has felt. A vamp following the Paradox Path that reaches 10 in the Path would feel proud of how &amp;quot;enlightned&amp;quot; he is, and would feel joy in how inhuman he has become. That's not personal terror, that's silly. That's like playing a merry demon that feels delighted in being evil.<br /> <br /> And Evil Revelations is an extreme case oviously, but there are many other paths that are just as evil but arent as reviled by the Kindred society and doesnt mean being hunted down, and that just as equally glorifies their inhuman monstruosity.<br /> <br /> The idea about the Humanity has always being about getting detached from your human condition, and slowly turn into a monster; that's the personal horror of it.<br /> <br /> If instead you become a happy monster, that's no longer a personal horror game, it just becomes a game of gore brutality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falling to wight is the obliteration of self, all self control, intellect and thought vanish into what is basically a permanent hunger frenzy, that is as horrific an idea for someone on Power and the Inner Voice, or Caine, or even Evil Revelations as it is for someone on Humanity. The way they maintain self control and ego, is different, but they all seek to be something more than a lobotomized hunger zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}